\tr{\td{con-leche}\td{3 x 6}\td{1.173 (1.165 - 1.184)}\td{1.185 (1.169 - 1.193)}\td{\strong{1.011}}\td{1.000 1.008 1.024}\td{1.207 (1.166 - 1.228)}\td{1.224 (1.202 - 1.245)}\td{\strong{1.014}}\td{0.997 1.015 1.031}\td{1.012}}
\tr{\td{navier-stokes-euler}\td{3 x 6}\td{3.000 (2.929 - 3.046)}\td{3.032 (2.976 - 3.071)}\td{\strong{1.011}}\td{1.041 0.983 1.008}\td{3.174 (3.159 - 3.201)}\td{3.186 (3.126 - 3.222)}\td{\strong{1.004}}\td{1.016 1.019 0.977}\td{1.007}}
\tr{\td{cslib}\td{3 x 6}\td{4.008 (3.978 - 4.027)}\td{4.021 (3.997 - 4.051)}\td{\strong{1.003}}\td{1.018 0.999 0.993}\td{4.357 (4.292 - 4.406)}\td{4.323 (4.281 - 4.371)}\td{\strong{0.992}}\td{0.997 0.987 0.992}\td{0.998}}
\tr{\td{mathlib}\td{3 x 4}\td{11.078 (10.982 - 11.223)}\td{11.075 (11.018 - 11.144)}\td{\strong{1.000}}\td{0.999 0.986 1.015}\td{12.061 (11.893 - 12.171)}\td{11.940 (11.857 - 12.067)}\td{\strong{0.990}}\td{0.978 1.015 0.978}\td{0.995}}
\tr{\td{\strong{geometric mean}}\td{}\td{}\td{}\td{\strong{1.007}}\td{0.996 to 1.019}\td{}\td{}\td{\strong{1.001}}\td{0.959 to 1.035}\td{\strong{1.004} (0.989 to 1.016)}}
}

\ul{
\li{\strong{With the launcher's flags the stock JDK is within 2 \% of the GraalVM JDK on every corpus}: from 0.4 \% faster (Init) to 1.9 \% slower (reachability), 0.7 \% slower in the geometric mean. Mathlib is 11.08 s on both, the number of [the merged build](rep-INT8) (11.00 s) on the day's distribution.}
\li{\strong{Without the advice}: 0.1 \% in the geometric mean, with Init 3.5 \% slower and reachability 4.1 \% faster on Temurin. Those are the two shortest passes (0.55 and 0.32 s), and one round each makes the cell: 1.102 on Init, 0.907 on reachability. Over both pairs, six rounds a corpus, every corpus is within 1.6 \% and the geometric mean is 1.004.}
\li{\strong{What three rounds resolve.} Of the 48 round ratios 41 are within 3 \% of 1, six are above 1.03 and one below 0.97; the median is 1.000. A cell of three rounds of a pass under a second is good to about 3 \%, as [the insight on interleaved rounds](ins-MBQS) says. The measurement shows no difference between the JDKs and cannot exclude one of about 1 \%.}
\li{\strong{With the other statistic}, the median of all later passes (2 to N), which the tables of [the default switch set](dec-YP0N) use and which includes passes in which the JIT still works: 1.016, 1.004, 1.039, 1.040, 1.007, 1.013, 1.004, 0.998 in the order of the table with the launcher's flags (geometric mean 1.015; cedar and reachability above 3 \%), and 1.031, 1.026, 0.988, 0.989, 1.008, 1.004, 0.993, 0.987 without the advice (1.003; Init above 3 \%); both pairs together 1.009, every corpus within 2.3 \%. The cells above 3 \% do not repeat in the other pair.}
}
}

