\li{\strong{About half of it is the huge-page advice}: without it the launcher's line is 4.9 \% slower on Temurin in the geometric mean (7.5 to 7.8 \% on cslib and Mathlib) and 5.5 \% on GraalVM CE (next table). The rest, serial against G1 and eight against four compiler threads, is 3.5 \%, most of it on reachability (13.9 \%).}
\li{This agrees with what [the launcher's flag line](rep-J1) and [the collector comparison](rep-GC) found on the GraalVM JDK: the reasons for the flags carry over to a stock JDK. G1 spends less time collecting on the large corpora (74 against 150 ms of a Mathlib pass) and holds more memory (5,800 against 5,172 MiB).}
